 image\" title=\"Diamond Ring\"><img alt=\"Diamond Ring\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/f5/D012_Phoenix_Down.png/revision/latest?cb=20120409211126\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"D012 Phoenix Down.png\"><img alt=\"D012 Phoenix Down.png\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"10\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Phoenix Down.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Phoenix_Down.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/f5/D012_Phoenix_Down.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/10?cb=20120409211126\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Imaginary Soldier\"><img alt=\"Imaginary Soldier\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As we enter we're contacted by a moogle, sadly not the mured moogle, he's in deeper. Yes, deeper, not a mere five-floors, this gateway is ten floors deep.\n</p><p>Multichain at C3 to get all enemies, this is the player to use a KP Gambler if you have one. The blue emblem is once again, accessories protect, lame.\n</p><p>Our first two new playmates are the Normal enemies, a Level 43 Imaginary Soldier and a Level 42 Delusory Knight. The comes the first Party piece, a Fallacious Tree with a Fallacious Wanderer Assist and an unknown summon, a Phantasmal Harlequin with Tiamat and a Phantasmal Girl Assist, and a Imaginary Champion with Bahamut and an Imaginary Soldier. The second Party consists of a Level 39 Fleeting Flash, Level 40 Ephemeral Summoner, and a Level 43 Transient Gunner. The red chest is another enemy, a Level 82 Capricious Reaper with a Capricious Thief Assist. In other words, the enemies down here are <i>about the same enemies you've mowed down since you first landed in Cornelia</i>. There are few things I hate more, kiddies, than walkthroughing something boring and repetitive.\n</p><p>The chest has a Diamond Ring. Approach the Moogle gives us the Moogle summon, with a variable cutscene upon receiving it. If she's in your party make Terra the party leader for some \"aaaaaaaaw\" lulz.\n</p><p>On this floor my entire party finally hit Level 100. When yours do, they should have all their attacks mastered at this point. Now focus on mastering the three Evasion Boost skills, Counterattack, Sneak Attack, First Strike, and then the four \"Exp to ----\" abilities. They do what they stay, instead of exp your character will get some HP, Bravery, Assist or EX Charge. Note EX to Bravery though is glitched when it comes to wall rush attacks, as there's a slight delay in its activation while your Bravery takes a second to drop to 0, and as a result Exp to Bravery only grants you Bravery based on the wall rush damage, not the base damage. For Cloud and others, this sucks, for Zidane and others, this is awesome. Just keep in mind the conversation is actually a conversion, so if you have party members below level 100 and the leader has an Exp to ---- ability equipped, the rest of the party gets no exp.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Depths_of_the_Earth\">The Depths of the Earth</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Depths of the Earth\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_24?action=edit&amp;section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Depths of the Earth\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/DFF_Rare_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=2011