 loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"KP +1\"><img alt=\"KP +1\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Purple.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Purple.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/13/D012_Emblem_Purple.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050509\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204003912\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"False Stalwart\"><img alt=\"False Stalwart\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"25\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Expert Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/25?cb=20110204003912\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110204003912\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Delusory Warlock\"><img alt=\"Delusory Warlock\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"25\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Expert Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/1/1e/DFF_Expert_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/25?cb=20110204003912\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Iifa Leaf\"><img alt=\"Iifa Leaf\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><b>AC</b>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Force of the Resolute Equipment piece\"><img alt=\"Force of the Resolute Equipment piece\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As we enter the moogle calls to us again and says once we unseal him, he wants us to go to that gateway he sealed. This is, in practice, the last floor.\n</p><p>The best way to chain enemies is a Straight Chain at G5. To get there, beat the enemy at E3 normally, then get your Assist out of the way and move to the square and use the chain.\n</p><p>First, fight the Level 39 Delusory Dragoon at C2. The chest it guards has a random skill and might give you a Straight Chain. I got a Multichain, just as good. Go fight the Level 43 Capricious Thief at E3, then open the chest at F5 to get an Iifa Leaf and open the path to your Assist. In the chain, first comes the Party piece, a Level 42 Fallacious Wanderer, a Level 42 Phantasmal Girl, and a Level 82 Ephemeral Phantom with Malboro and an Ephemeral Vision as Assist. Then comes a Level 80 False Stalwart with Behemoth and a False Hero Assist, and a Level 81 Delusory Warlock with, shock and surprise, Giant of Babil and a Delusory Knight.\n</p><p>Grab the final chests, another skill and a random Force of the Resolute equipment piece. It's another 4-piece set of equipment you don't care about and don't want, it grants +30% EX Force Absorption and converts EX Force and EX Cores to Bravery. And is Level 30.\n</p><p>On the final floor, you can head right to the moogle, or open the red chest knowing it's an enemy - a Level 80 Fallacious Tree with a Fallacious Wanderer Assist - to get the two chests for more trade accessories.\n</p><p>As we reach the end, the seal on the mured moogle is undone! We get notification of a new Report with a fight to have fun with, then we reappear on the world map with the mured moogle following us from now on. He directs us to Crescent Lake, but first we have stops to make.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Release_the_Seals\">Release the Seals</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Release the Seals\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_24?action=edit&amp;section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Release the Seals\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Terra is going to lead the way now, I bought her an Empyrean Rod for a stronger weapon, and also bought her a Royal Crown, a Level 100 Hairpin, it cost me a lot and I had to resort to selling Battlegen items, but it's the principle of the thing. I also could have bought Prishe the Ehrgeiz, a Level 100 grappling weapon, but I needed way too much cash for both. Lightning and Cloud got the Kazekiri\n</p><p>Teleport to Cornelia and head to the Gateway to Departure. The seals in the gateways will be unlocked now, and we can access the chest with 30,000 gil...hm, maybe I should have come here first. Then teleport to the Elven Castle and head east. Also note you can find Tifa near the castle and Kain near the Gulg Volcano, they say a line and the vanish. Spooky. Go to the Gateway of Melting Sorrows and take the unsealed chest for a Pink Tail. Beyond at the Gateway of the Great Will, there's another sealed chest with a Pink Tail. Head up into the volcano area now and down the hill into the Encounters and Treason gateway, the sealed chest, of course, has a Pink Tail.\n</p><p>Now teleport to Crescent Lake and go north into the Cornelia Plains. Go north, shatter the rock to get to a Diamond, and approach the gateway - this is the sealed gateway the mured moogle was directing us too.\n</p><p>Equip everyone with the best equipment you have, and the following accessories - Hyper Ring, Muscle Belt/Earring, HP = 100%, Near Loss, BRV ≥ Base Value, Summon Used, Pre-EX Mode, Pre-EX Revenge, (Opp) HP ≥ 10000, and (Opp) Empty Assist Gauge. For summons, get stuff like Bahamut, Behemoth, Brynhildr, and Tiamat on everyone - essentially whatever gives you a massive Bravery boost. Also give them all the Cat Nip ability, the three Evasion Boost abilities, and if you have the CP, Counterattack. An Exp to ---- would be nice, but unless you've mastered one it costs too much CP.\n</p><p>Head inside, and prepare for what is easily the most powerful enemy you've yet faced.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"God_in_Fire\">God in Fire</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: God in Fire\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_24?action=edit&amp;section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: God in Fire\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Feral_Chaos\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Feral Chaos\">Feral Chaos</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/4e/DesperadoChaosAltRender.png/revision/latest?cb=20120417041840\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DesperadoChaosAltRender\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"171\" height=\"200\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DesperadoChaosAltRender.png\" data-image-key=\"DesperadoChaosAltRender.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/4/4e/DesperadoChaosAltRender.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/171?cb=20120417041840\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">59,996\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">95\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">966\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Snarl, Spew, Brute Force, Raid\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Deus Iratus, Ventus Ire, Lux Magnus\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Shinryu Verus\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">3/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Behold Feral Chaos, a grotesquely deformed form of Chaos and a preview of the game's true final boss.\n</p><p>His Bravery attacks are Snarl, a quick two-hit slash on the ground, Spew, where he jumps up and slams the ground to create plumes of fire beneath you, Brute Force, a diving claw combo in the air, and Raid, where he descends rapidly to unleash a shockwave when he stops. All of Feral Chaos's Bravery attacks wall rush or chase, depending on if you hit the wall too soon or not. Snarl and Spew can be blocked, but Brute Force and Raid cannot. Brute Force is his most used attack, it crushes your guards, has a good range for it, and does a lot of damage. \n</p><p>His HP attacks are Deus Iratus, where on the ground he blocks attacks and creates a ring of fire around him, Ventus Ire, where he angles up or down and then flaps his wings towards you to send out a gust of air, and Lux Magnus, where he shoots a beam of fire straight down in the air and can move to track you down. Deus Iratus can be avoided by simply not attacking him on the ground, while Lux Magnus, just keep dodging away. Ventus Ire is a bit trickier, dodge away but if you don't do it fast enough he'll hit you, since Feral Chaos likes using Ventus Ire after wall rushing you. Feral Chaos's summon is Shinryu Verus, which copies the effects of the four fiend summons - Bravery freeze on you, Bravery swap, sap Bravery to 0, or triple his Bravery. And no that is not a typo, he has almost 60,000 HP.\n</p><p>The true difficulty of this fight is Feral Chaos's accessories. He has Door to Despair, which gives him a 5% damage and defense boost, and Tyranny of Darkness, giving him 5% EX and Assist depletion. And then he has Waking Darkness, which after 60 seconds activates for a <i><b>90x multiplier</b></i>. Suddenly Feral Chaos's attacks are obscenely strong, he takes probably no damage from your attacks, and every HP attack depletes your Assist and EX Gauges to 0. Thus you effectively only have 60 seconds to fight, after that he will easily Break you and get 9999 Bravery with one Brute Force, and the next HP attack will kill you.\n</p><p>Now, when it comes to rating Feral Chaos's difficulty, I must admit I personally have trouble with this. Anyone who follows me on YouTube knows I (at least I like to think so) have made a reputation killing him over and over and over. So I'm familiar with how his AI works and how to avoid and counter his attacks. This Feral Chaos doesn't fight quite the same as the real thing I'm used to, but the lessons stick. All you really need to do is get used to dodging his attacks. Brute Force is actually pretty easy to dodge once you learn how to see it ocming, and Deus Iratus and Ventus Ire, just keep your distance, which is why I brought Terra. <i>Normally</i> his defenses are too high to damage, but at 9999 Bravery the critical hit multiplier does 8x normal damage, so your critical hits will still hurt a bit. Otherwise when that booster goes off, just rely on HP attacks and only do Bravery attack to charge up your Assist. This is the one time I would consider using Resin-type items, but I didn't. And Terra's Kraken summon swapped my 0 Bravery (got an HP hit just before the timer) with his 9999, awesome.\n</p><p>You have the entire party to share the burden, the only factor is if you think the current member did enough HP damage, because the remaining people have to share the rest. Also just keep in mind boosters don't work in EX Bursts, so feel free to go for the EX Burst finish as usual. Otherwise, just good luck, learn to predict his Brute Force and HP attacks, dodge them and counter, and you'll be just fine.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"To_the_Desert\">To the Desert</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: To the Desert\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_24?action=edit&amp;section=5\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: To the Desert\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/2/2b/World_B_Mirage_Sandsea.png/revision/latest?cb=20110505202957\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Mirage Sandsea\"><img alt=\"Mirage Sandsea\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"260\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"World B Mirage Sandsea.png\" data-image-key=\"World_B_Mirage_Sandsea.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/2/2b/World_B_Mirage_Sandsea.png/revision/latest?cb=20110505202957\" /></a><figcaption>Mirage Sandsea</figcaption></figure>\n<p>With Feral Chaos vanquished, the gateway is automatically unsealed, and we get notification of a new Report. I recommend doing it now, along with Report 18 if you haven't already. The two fights here unlock the ability to Battlegen from Prishe and Gilgamesh, Battlegen items from them are needed for many Level 60 and 90 equipment pieces, as well as the Level 100 Genji equipment, so when you encounter their Manikins from now on you'll want to get your hands on the spoils they cough up.\n</p><p>Now on the world map, if you want to go back and look, Yuna, Terra and Prishe can be found wandering about, if they aren't your current party leader, and they have some pretty depressing things to say to you. For this next segment, Zidane is my party leader. Head north to find a rock to smash to reach an island with a Diamond, and a teleport stone. There are several new locations on the map we can go to, but let's go by land for now. Continue north, and after a short time, you'll come to the Forgotten Trail gateway.\n<br style=\"clear:both\" />\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/DFF_Rare_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235927\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"30,000 Gil\"><img alt=\"30,000 Gil\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Rare Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Rare_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/6/6b/DFF_Rare_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203235927\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ac/D012_Emblem_Red.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209050655\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Magic Damage 0\"><img alt=\"Magic Damage 0\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"D012 Emblem Red.png\" data-image-key=\"D012_Emblem_Red.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/a/ac/D012_Emblem_